    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for the Austin Waves centers on capitalizing against favorable starting pitching, with **Miguel Vargas** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** emerging as our strongest plays. **Miguel Vargas** (63.53) benefits significantly from facing Abbott, who carries an inflated 5.02 xERA, allowing **Miguel Vargas** to leverage his elite 0.381 xwOBA into a primary run-producing role in the three-hole. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (60.95) remains a pillar of the offense; despite facing the tough Tolle, his dynamic platoon advantage as a right-handed bat against a lefty starter keeps his efficiency well within the \"Strong\" start threshold. These two will be the primary engines for our RBI and run production tonight.\n\nThe bench composition is dictated by a lack of volume, as **Gunnar Henderson**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jackson Merrill** are all off today, and **Jordan Westburg** remains sidelined on the IL. This lack of depth makes the situational efficiency of the starters critical. **Wade Meckler** (42.25) presents the most notable risk in the outfield; while he secures a lead-off spot against deGrom\u2014an elite arm with a 3.13 xERA\u2014his floor is suppressed by the pitching matchup. We are strictly chasing his speed and run-scoring potential here, as he barely cleared our internal threshold for a start. Conversely, **Sam Antonacci** (47.00) faces a challenging platoon disadvantage against Abbott, which aggressively dragged his score down. We are starting him out of necessity to ensure we are not wasting a game cap, but he serves as our most vulnerable link in the batting order. We are proceeding with caution as the pitching matchups, specifically the facing of deGrom, introduce significant volatility to our daily offensive output.",
